---
import Layout from "../../components/Layout.astro";
import DocShell from "../../components/DocShell.astro";
import CommandBlock from "../../components/CommandBlock.astro";
---

<Layout title="Quickstart | ArkheionX Docs" description="A short ArkheionX workflow from environment check to review package.">
  <DocShell>
    <p class="page-kicker">Start</p>
    <h1>Quickstart.</h1>
    <p class="doc-deck">A compact sequence for producing and inspecting a local review surface.</p>

    <h2>Check the command</h2>
    <CommandBlock command={`arkheionx version
arkheionx doctor .`} />

    <h2>Orient the repository</h2>
    <CommandBlock command={`arkheionx open .
arkheionx map .
arkheionx flow .`} />
    <p><code>open</code> provides a compact orientation. <code>map</code> expands roles and journeys. <code>flow</code> focuses on candidate money-flow edges.</p>

    <h2>Build focused review artifacts</h2>
    <CommandBlock command={`arkheionx review-map .
arkheionx value-paths .
arkheionx assumptions .
arkheionx test-gap-map .
arkheionx evidence-links .`} />

    <h2>Package the current state</h2>
    <CommandBlock command={`arkheionx validate-artifacts .
arkheionx review-package . --strict`} />
    <p>The package collects existing local artifacts, writes a manifest and validation report, and can be regenerated from the same repository state.</p>

    <h2>Inspect before extending execution</h2>
    <p>
      Stop and read the generated map before using commands with <code>--build</code> or <code>--run</code>. Those flags can invoke local Foundry
      operations. They remain explicit because execution changes the evidence and trust boundary.
    </p>
  </DocShell>
</Layout>
